In general this may be true, but is not universal.  For instance, some
if not all DLT 4000 drives can read and write DLT III, DLT IIIXT and 
DLT-IV tapes.  It depends on what firmware is loaded into the drive as
to what densities and tapes are supported, the hardware sometimes will
support more than the firmware.

