Joe,

Your best bet is to contact Evergreen and ask them the question before you buy.
DEC stuck with Intel Pentium chips all the way with the Celebris GL5xxxx and
GL5xxxx-st, so if BIOS compatibility with a non-Intel CPU is an issue, you
cannot count on a DEC BIOS upgrade to help you.  Also the Celebris GL5xxxx
series predates the design of the AMD K6 CPU on which the Spectra upgrade is
based.  Evergreen provided AMD CPU compatibility BIOS upgrades for a limited
number of motherboards.  So ask Evergreen if you don't hear back from someone in
this newsgroup.

I have successfully upgraded later DEC Celebris and Venturis models with AMD
chips, but all the DEC models seem to have been done by vastly different
engineering groups with not a lot of effective communication between them.

Believe it or not, you can still find the DEC info on the HPaq web site,
somewhere deep in the Compaq archives if you look hard enough.  If there is a
BIOS upgrade for your model of computer, it would be there.  For how long?
Well, if Carly gets motivated, all the once DEC stuff could be gone tomorrow.

... Ben Myers

