Konstantin Klubnichkin wrote:

> Hi !
>
> Now I've got couple of CompactTapeIII (TK85?) and couple of CompactTape
> (TK50?) cartridges.
>
> As far as I understand it's impossible to R/W TK85 in TK70 drive if tape
> was previosly initialized in TK85 drive? Is it right? Is it really
> impossible to re-init tape?

    When a blank tape is loaded for the first time in <any> TZ70,
85,86,87,88 or 89, the drive writes some formatting information at
the beginning of the tape (you might call this "initializing", but
not in the sense of the VMS INITIALIZE command, more like writing
some sort of tracking information...).  When an initialized tape
is loaded in any of these drives, they first read that information
in order to know how to READ/WRITE the tape, i.e., that's how a
TZ87 knows how to read a TK70 tape, or a how TK70 knows how to read
a TK50 tape (examples, I don't have the compatibility matrix in
front of me).

    You can initialize a previously written tape _only_ if the
drive thinks it's blank.  Therefore, subject the tape to a good
bulk eraser and you'll be set. :-)  I think...  I've certainly
erased TK50 tapes and initialized them on TK70's.  I'm not so
sure that a CompactTape III is physically compatible with a
TK70, but it's certainly worth a try.

    -Ken
--
I don't speak for Intel, Intel doesn't speak for me...

