> Hi !
> 
> Now I've got couple of CompactTapeIII (TK85?) and couple of CompactTape 
> (TK50?) cartridges.
> 
> As far as I understand it's impossible to R/W TK85 in TK70 drive if tape 
> was previosly initialized in TK85 drive? Is it right? Is it really 
> impossible to re-init tape?
> 
> Thanx!
> 
> P.S. Got old broken VT420, playing around. It makes sounds like 
> heartbeat, looks like power supply is dead :(

Sounds like the power suply cutting out because of an overload.

VT's >= 220 have low quality flyback transformers and usually that
goes first.  On the 220/320's it would actually crack open and leak
brown ooze (which then hardens).

Another thing to check is the connectors, I've seen
several of the connectors that have actually fried and/or welded
themselves (usually from the tube to the main board) (poor
connection I'd guess).

Sometimes the tube goes bad.  Unplug the connector from the
base of the CRT and see if it powers up ok.




