On Wed, Aug 28, 2002; "Ian King" <iking@killthewabbit.org> wrote:

> Does anyone out there have a DECserver 300 power supply?  I bought a DS on
> eBay (cheap), and its power supply is obviously toast.  (Fortunately, the
> documentation I got with it was worth what I paid.)  I've had little success
> fixing switching supplies in the past (usually finding components is the
> biggest obstacle), so if someone has perhaps a dead DS300 with a good power
> supply, can we make a deal?

In a sense, yes.  I opened up both a DECserver 200/MC and a 300.  Although
I could not find a DEC p/n on the power supply, the mfr's p/n is on the
circuit board and they are the same for both models.

In fact the fan assembly, the cable from the power supply to the main board,
the AUI cable from the mainboard to the back panel, and the two cables from
the main board to the interface board all have matching part numbers.  In
other words, the 200 is a great source of parts for a 300.

The irony in this is that I gutted a 200 last year to use the case for
a homebrew project.  I don't think I kept the guts since I have other
200s sitting around.  I will have a look around to see if I did kept the
power supply.  Failing that and if you can't find another source, I guess
I could pull a power supply from a 200 for you.  Contact me direct if
you're interested.

HTH,
Mike Thompson



