Hi ppl!

Last night had nice time with my uVax-3800.
 From the begining. I have uVAX-3800 with 110V power supply. But here in 
Russia we have 220V in outlets so I've bought transformer 220->110 and 
powered VAXen up. As it noted on PSU it can consume up to 670Watt and my 
  transformer can bring only 630Watt, so I have some kind of 
power-bottle-neck in my home lab.
I've had strange problem with VAXen - sometimes without any visible 
reason it falls into reset state and fails to pass system test 
(sometimes it resets again at test #23, sometimes at #13). So my guess 
was cards in computer consume too much. So let me show you original 
configuration:
 From right to left:
PSU
KA655
Two memory banks
DPV-11
DESQA-SA
CXA16-M
empty
empty(not shure, forgot total number of slots)
TQK70 (TK70 drive)
KFQSA (2xRF71 drives)
empty
empty
PSU
First thing to do was to remove unused DPV11 and CXA16-M. I've done this 
  and.... ">>>sho dev" showed no disks at all.
After that I've had about 2 hours of sex with slow connect to Internet 
from my book, tossing boards, etc etc etc.
Finally I've found on some FAQ that KFQSA can be reprogrammed.
I've put switches to "service 0" position, typed
 >>> set host/maintenance/uqssp/service 0, VAXen answered with:
UQSSP Controller (774420)
 >>>
Oops. Than another 2 hours of you-know-what.
Than I've just placed both controllers (KFQSA and TQK70) just near of 
memory banks and it begun to live.

Looks like there issue with Qbus load and parasite capacities made by 
that cards (CXA16 and DPV-11) but it looks _very_ strange.

OK, now it works. I can see both HDs and tape and network.

Just one quiestion still exist:
When I programm KFQSA in service mode how do I know CSRs of hard 
drives??? Couldnt find any info last night.

Thats all folks. Sorry if it is well-known issues :)

Best regards,
Konstantin Klubnichkin



