Konstantin Klubnichkin wrote:
> powered VAXen up. As it noted on PSU it can consume up to 670Watt and my
> transformer can bring only 630Watt,

Since you have depopulated the Q-bus slots, the whole computer probably won't
consume the full 670W.

> First thing to do was to remove unused DPV11 and CXA16-M. I've done this
> and.... ">>>sho dev" showed no disks at all.

Careful there!  If you remove cards from a Q-bus machine, you may have to
reconfigure the remaining cards or the O/S may not recognize them.  What O/S do
you intend to run?  VMS?

> Than I've just placed both controllers (KFQSA and TQK70) just near of
> memory banks and it begun to live.

This sounds as though you have no bus-grant cards.  All slots on the Q-bus
should be filled with either controllers or bus-grant cards.  Possibly it will
work if all cards are placed together (since working cards pass the bus-grant
signals for cards farther away from the CPU).

> Just one quiestion still exist:
> When I programm KFQSA in service mode how do I know CSRs of hard
> drives??? Couldnt find any info last night.

I have no idea, but DSSI disks are intelligent drives that act as their own
cluster node, respond to queries, etc.  First make sure that they all have a
different node address from each other and the controller, and you should be
able to see them with a

>>> show device

command at the console prompt.

 - JB


