> So, I installed a TGA board, a PC keyboard and monitor, and tried to
> boot the system. I didn't get much output, just a black screen with a
> still cursor. After a while, trying many keys combinations, I found
> that CTRL-X would give me the SRM prompt. Any idea why ?

Your first clue was the absense of a graphics card, so it was a server in
it's previous life.  Without a graphics card, the only way to talk to it
was via a serial line and a terminal emulator.  If you hadn't tried
activating the ARC console (AlphaBios) the fix is easy, at the SRM prompt
>>> type:
>>>set console graphics  (might be different in your system)
And Viola! you have graphics (assuming that the graphics card you have is
supported by your system, tell us more about the TGA card that you have)

Too bad you tried the ARC (AlphaBios) console. It will get complicated
now.
Now you've got to set up a terminal and hook it to the serial line, get
the computer back into SRM and then reset the Console global.

Hopefully someone here will be able to walk you through the steps as I've
never played with a 500/333 in AlphaBios mode.

Good luck!

TomC



