Jim wrote:
> I've just been passed an Alpha Server 400 and I'm *trying* to install
> an OS on it
> Anyone tell me how to boot from either the fdd or the cdrom ?
> I've tried all the typical Sun commands ie boot cdrom, boot sd(0,0,0)
> and just about everything I could think of but to no avail !

I assume that if you are typing in commands that you have it set
to the srm console. Good.
The srm console is used for booting VMS or Tru64, to install and
boot windows nt you would use the Arc console, but I don't know
enough details about it to talk you through an Arc install.

Assuming you want to install a real OS and not NT, then read on.

To boot from cdrom you need to find out the device identifier for
the cdrom device.

At the >>> prompt type show dev to see which devices you have installed.
One of them will be the cdrom.
The device name will be related to the scsi bus and target that the device
is installed on, for example devices on the first bus will be dkaxxx the
second will be dkbxxx etc.
Typically in an as400 the cdrom is dka400 (scsi id 4 on the first bus), so
