  My experience with the under-revision VCB02/GPX/Dragon controller
  on the faster processors was also a "benign" Q-bus bus hang.

  There are other timing issues which can keep a down-revision VCB02
  from functioning, as well.  (If you occasionally don't get video
  synch when powering up or you get a bus hang, you've probably got
  a down-revision module.)

  With the KA650 (MicroVAX 3500, VAXstation 3200, etc) and the KA660
  (VAX 4000 model 200), you'll want (need) revision C1 (or later) for
  the VCB02 M7169 base module and revision A2 (or later) for each of
  the M7168 "planes" modules installed.  (Revision requirements for 
  other VAXstation processors can differ.)


