"Aus, Hans Magnus" wrote:
> 
> How do I change the booted console to SRM?

There are two ways.

1)

From the AlphaBios boot screen press F2 to enter SETUP.

Select the "CMOS Setup..." entry.

In the "CMOS Setup" screen, press F6 for Advanced Options.

In the "Advanced CMOS Setup" screen, tab down to the
"Console Selection:" line. Use the UP/DOWN arrow keys to select
the desired operating system console (SRM or AlphaBios).
F10 will save your changes.

Once your changes have been saved press the machine's restart button
or power cycle the machine. It will now startup in the SRM console.


2)

When the machine is initializing, either at power up or when the
RESTART button is pressed, press and hold in the HALT switch. The
machine will trap to the SRM console to complain that it can't
start the AlphaBios console.

At the SRM >>> prompts enter:

   >>> set auto_action halt
   >>> set os_type unix          (or VMS as desired)
   >>> init

That's all it takes.

At the SRM's >>> prompt enter "help" or "man" to see the commands 
available to you

