except USB.  Parallel thruput sucks, but it's easy to hitch up a parallel ZIP to
almost any computer in an emergency.

Product quality in the computer industry is simply too damned low for removable
media to succeed at high recording densities, and the drives are too fragile for
consumer use... Ben Myers

