>>for any of this graphic hardware??  Did any of the PDP OSes ever support
>>any kind of graphics beyond things like Tek-4010's??

>Hmm, now what do I remember playing moonlander on? A GT05 or
>something. Memory mapped, not raster image like a T4010. 

The GT40 (which was based on the PDP-11/05) was not a memory-mapped
video, it was a vector graphics engine (the VT11).  The instructions
were in main memory, but the VT11 processor would rescan the display
file (the instructions in memory) on a regular basis to redisplay
the image.  Large amounts of display data resulted in really bad
flicker because of the phosphor persistence.  Parts of an image could
be fading as other parts were re-drawn.

The advantage of this was that motion could be accomplished pretty
easily by changing the memory file... the display processor would
catch the change on the next refresh.

