In article <uljeb5f9tfef9d@corp.supernews.com>, sword7@speakeasy.org writes:
:In comp.os.vms Hoff Hoffman <hoffman@xdelta.zko.dec.nospam> wrote:
:>   I would target the VCB02, and not the VCB01.  I would only target 
:>   the VCB03 if you plan on providing a fully-capable SMP emulator.
:
:Ok, thank you for info.  I will use VCB02 for my emulator.   I know
:about VCB01 and VCB02.  I never heard of VCB03 before.  What is difference 
:between VCB02 and VCB03?

  The VCB03 is the graphics controller that was built for the Firefox
  series M-Bus.  VCB03 is capable of 1280 by 1024 at 66 Hz resolution,
  and provided 3D hardware acceleration and (when fully configured)
  24-bit true color.

  The Firefox M-bus was the main I/O bus on the VAXstation 3520 and
  VAXstation 3540 series SMP systems, though the systems did have an
  optional (and support-restricted) Q-bus expansion option available.

  Firefox was based on the CVAX series VAX microprocessor, and was
  available in two configurations; as a two-processor (3520) and as
  a four-processor (3540) version.


