Back when I had a lab with VAXen, I added VCB02s to KA650, KA655
and KA640 based systems. I had rev D and above base modules and
never saw lock-ups. But then again, it's only relatively recently
that I realised there might be an issue! I don't have a rev 
matrix for the VCB02 (or even the VAXstation 3200) so I cannot
tell you what the latest rev might be.


I am fairly sure, however, that the rev that fixed the bus lockup
fixed it for all the fast processors (where fast = faster than 
uVAX II). So if it works in a KA650, it should work in a KA694.

Also AFAIK, if it fails, it just locks the bus (i.e. the machine
hangs). It does not (again AFAIK) let out magic smoke.

