> not to turn the U.S. into a nation of burger flippers.

Not at all, since the only people who will turn the U.S. into a nation of
burger flippers are the U.S. work force, by failing to compete effectively
at anything more remunerative.  As I said previously, I don't believe U.S.
workers have any God-given right to their standard of living:  I think they
deserve it only if they earn it.  The fact that by something of a historical
accident this may have been less necessary in the past than it's becoming
now may have spoiled us somewhat, but that's our problem, not anyone else's:
we should be thankful for the advantages it has given us rather than
resentful that this inequity may be coming to an end.

- bill





